# RME manual pricing authority (rule 194)

> **SUPERSEDED IN PART by rule 195 (ACTIVATION-RME-INVOICE-CORRECTION-PREPAYMENT-2,
> 2026-10-21).** Owner D1a: the checker's approval APPLIES the correction in the
> same transaction. Owner D1b: Kasir requests, Admin Klinik approves, Front Office
> holds both — granted through `RoleSeeder`; no operational role holds
> `apply_rme_invoice_correction` (recovery path only). Owner D1c: the capability is
> confined to SPN4 by a source-controlled, fail-closed allowlist. Any statement
> below that "no role" holds a correction permission, that D1a is undecided, or that
> an approval leaves the invoice untouched until a separate apply is the historical
> record of its release, not current policy. D21c and D21g remain PENDING.

Evidence: `docs/sprints/revision-rme-manual-pricing-authority-1.md`.
Decision register: `docs/decisions/rme-billing-correction-owner-decisions.md` (D21 CURRENT).
**Supersedes the mandatory-tariff parts of rules 190 §2(11), 191 §4, 192 §1(4)/§2/§3/§4/§5/§7/§11(39)
and rule 193's strict-eligibility framing.** Where this rule and those disagree about PRICE
AUTHORITY, this rule wins. Their D1, D7, D10, Rp0, maker-checker, concurrency and tariff-provisioning
content stays in force.

## 1. Owner decision — D21 REVISED (OWNER_APPROVED_REVISED, recorded 2026-10-20)
1. There is **no mandatory official treatment tariff**. The authorized cashier types the price of every
   line of the ORIGINAL invoice. A price may differ between branches and between patients.
2. Recorded from task-supplied owner evidence (the brief), exactly like D1/D7/D10/D21 on 2026-10-17.
   Owner approval ≠ repository record ≠ technical enforcement — claim the third only with deployed,
   verified evidence. Never invent a sub-decision.

## 2. Superseded tariff policy (LEGACY_SUPERSEDED)
3. Withdrawn: "prices come from the branch tariff master", tariff equality, "correction only within tariff
   authority" (old D21(4)), the `CORRECTION_TARIFF_*` refusals, STALE `TARIFF_AUTHORITY_CHANGED`, the
   TRANSITIONAL mode as a "temporary" state, and the strict-readiness activation prerequisite.
4. Superseded text in older rules is MARKED, never deleted; historical rows keep their values.

## 3. Manual original invoice pricing (IMPLEMENTED)
5. `RmeInvoicePricingService::price()` — MANUAL for every branch: the cashier price is kept after server
   validation; **no tariff is read, compared, recorded or prefilled** on this path (tested: zero
   `mst_tariffs` queries).
6. The cashier form carries no tariff (`data-tariff` removed) and never prefills a price; it shows a
   manual-pricing notice (`data-pricing-authority="MANUAL_CASHIER_ENTRY"`). The display total is computed in
   integer cents; the SERVER total is the only stored one.

## 4. Optional tariff master
7. `mst_tariffs`, its approval provenance, `rme:tariff-authority-readiness`, `rme:tariff-template`,
   `rme:tariff-import` and master-data CRUD stay — as OPTIONAL REFERENCE. They never block or change
   billing. Never delete tariff rows or rewrite historical tariff amounts. No cross-branch fallback.

## 5. Branch-independent amounts
8. The same treatment may be billed at different amounts per branch and per patient. Branch scope of the
   INVOICE is still authoritative and server-derived (the visit's branch; a submitted `branch_id` is
   never read).

## 6. Server-side monetary validation (IMPLEMENTED)
9. Integer cents only (no float arithmetic). Unit price REQUIRED: empty / null / whitespace / exponent /
   thousands separators / currency text / 3+ decimals / non-finite ⇒ `INVOICE_AMOUNT_INVALID` — malformed
   money is never silently zero. qty ≥ 1 and ≤ `MAX_QTY` (2 147 483 647 — the PostgreSQL `integer`
   STORAGE bound, not a business cap; FormRequest `max:` + in-service `INVOICE_QTY_OVERFLOW`); price,
   discount ≥ 0; overflow of decimal(15,2) ⇒ `INVOICE_TOTAL_OVERFLOW` (refused per line BEFORE
   multiplying, so no product becomes a float, and again on the running total); totals recomputed;
   submitted totals ignored. Ordinary validation failures are 422s, never 500s.
10. A named treatment must exist, not be soft-deleted, and be active ⇒ else `INVOICE_TREATMENT_INVALID`
    (audited `RME_INVOICE_PRICING_REFUSED`, ids + code only). Free-text lines (no treatment) stay
    permitted — a live cashier workflow (production invoice 37).

## 7. Manual price provenance (IMPLEMENTED)
11. New lines: `pricing_mode = MANUAL`; `price_source` ∈ {`MANUAL_CASHIER_ENTRY`, `MANUAL_FREE_TEXT`,
    `CORRECTION_MANUAL_ENTRY`}; `tariff_id` / `tariff_unit_price` NULL. A manual price is NEVER labelled
    `TARIFF_MATCHED` (or any tariff label), even when it equals a tariff — coincidence is not authority.
12. Who/when is recorded by the invoice (cashier, created_at) and the correction (maker/checker/applier) —
    not duplicated on the line. Historical values (NULL, `TARIFF_*`, `TRANSITIONAL_*`) are never
    backfilled or rewritten; they render with honest historical labels.

## 8. Discount boundary
13. A discount is NOT a manual unit price. Enforced: `0 ≤ discount ≤ line gross` ⇒ no negative line or
    total (`INVOICE_LINE_NEGATIVE` / `CORRECTION_LINE_NEGATIVE`). **No percentage or amount cap and no
    discount approver are invented — D21c is PENDING_SUB_DECISION.**

## 9. Issued invoice immutability
14. After creation an RME invoice and its items are never edited directly: no edit/update/delete route
    exists for them (pinned by a route-table test); only `RmeInvoiceCorrectionService` may call
    `updateItem` / `deleteItem` / `createItem` / `applyCorrectionTotals` (pinned by a source scan).

## 10. Correction workflow requirement
15. Every change to an issued invoice goes through the correction workflow: request → approve → apply
    (maker ≠ checker), pre-payment only, branch-scoped, audited, version + fingerprint checked.

## 11. Maker-checker (D1, unchanged)
16. Kasir submits; Admin Klinik approves within its branch; Super Admin across branches; nobody — Super
    Admin included — approves their own request (enforced in the service under the lock, not the policy).
    D1a (who APPLIES) is undecided — never invent it. **[Rule 195: D1a DECIDED 2026-10-21 — the checker's approval applies, atomically.]**

## 12. Document versioning (D7, unchanged)
17. v0 original frozen on first apply; v1… immutable revisions; SHA-256; nothing overwritten; no paid
    receipt for an unpaid invoice; no refund evidence without a refund.

## 13. Payment blocking (D10, unchanged)
18. An invoice with a SUBMITTED / APPROVED-not-applied correction accepts no payment on any path
    (`pay`, `allocateControlPayment`, `allocateVisitPayment`), checked on the locked row, whole batch
    rolled back; payment forms bound to `invoice_versions[...]` = `correction_version` (rule 191).

## 14. Correction tariff-independence (IMPLEMENTED)
19. A corrected price may differ from the original and from any tariff; a branch with no tariff corrects
    normally. `RmeInvoiceCorrectionService` holds no tariff dependency (pinned by a source scan).

## 15. Correction approval validation
20. Approval re-locks invoice → correction and re-runs staleness: invoice removed, payment recorded,
    status changed, version changed, content fingerprint changed, lab candidates — **never a tariff**.

## 16. Correction application validation
21. Apply re-checks the same staleness under the lock, writes changed/added lines as
    `CORRECTION_MANUAL_ENTRY` / `MANUAL`, recomputes totals, refuses if the applied total differs from the
    approved total, and is idempotent (re-apply = no-op).

## 17. Rp0 boundary
22. Original invoice: pre-revision behaviour kept (Rp0 accepted, audited as `zero_value_lines`) — no new
    Rp0 privilege and no new Rp0 block (D21g / D11 / D22 pending). Correction: every NEW Rp0 line or total
    refused (`CORRECTION_RP0_NOT_PERMITTED`), consultation included. The approved Rp0 ADJUSTMENT scope
    (Kontrol / Konsultasi Dokter, rule 188 §12) is a separate, NOT built workflow — `RP0_ADJUSTMENT=NOT_ACTIVE`.
    **[FORWARD 2026-11-01 — rule 217]** Built as a CLOSURE, not a correction: a legitimate Rp0 Konsultasi /
    Kontrol invoice can be closed `NO_CHARGE` ("Selesai Tanpa Biaya", flag OFF). A correction still never
    creates a Rp0 line or total, and manual pricing at issuance is unchanged.

## 18. Existing Rp0 legacy preservation
23. Historical Rp0 invoices (production #36, `TRT-CONS`, UNPAID) are never deleted or rewritten.

## 19. Payment immutability
24. `RmePayment` refuses Eloquent update (except patient_id) and delete (rule 189). Manual pricing never
    writes a payment, a reversal, a refund or a credit balance.

## 20. Invoice version safety
25. Every payment path compares `invoice_versions[id]` to the locked `correction_version` (rule 191).

## 21. Financial audit logging
26. `RME_INVOICE_CREATED` (inside the invoice transaction) carries `pricing_mode` and per-source line
    counts (`lines_manual_cashier_entry`, `lines_manual_free_text`, …) + `zero_value_lines`; never a
    patient name, RM number, NIK, clinical note or payment reference.

## 22. Branch isolation
27. Cashier scope = `RmeWorkingBranchScope`; the invoice branch = the visit's branch; correction actors are
    branch-scoped in the service. No price endpoint exposes another branch's invoice.
27a. **Issuing an invoice is branch-bounded too** (security review F1, fixed here):
    `RmeInvoicePolicy::create(User, ?ClinicVisit)` applies the working-branch scope, both
    `rme.cashier.create` / `rme.cashier.store` authorize WITH the visit, and
    `RmeInvoiceService::create()` re-checks `allows($cashier, $visit->branch_id)` on the LOCKED visit
    (403). A context-bound cashier with no working branch fails closed; a whole-estate role is
    unaffected. Under manual pricing the typed price is the financial snapshot — never let a cashier
    type one for another branch's visit.

## 23. Clinical data separation
28. Pricing never writes medical records, diagnoses, odontograms, consent, visits' clinical content or
    doctor attribution; a correction can never re-attribute an existing line's doctor.

## 24–26. Oversight roles
29. Finance Klinik and Data Analyst stay READ-ONLY (rule 186); laboratory `Finance` is untouched.

## 27. Feature flag governance
30. `FEATURE_RME_INVOICE_CORRECTION` stays **OFF**; the three operational correction permissions stay
    granted to NO role. Strict pricing and price exceptions stay OFF (source-controlled; no environment
    key can enable either). Post-payment correction, refund and Rp0 adjustment are NOT_ACTIVE.

## 28. Refund restrictions
31. Nothing here refunds, reverses or credits. Refund execution remains unbuilt (rule 189).

## 29–30. PostgreSQL concurrency & idempotency
32. Lock order unchanged (invoice row, then correction row). D10 races and correction apply idempotency stay
    proven on PostgreSQL 16 by `RmeInvoiceCorrectionConcurrencyTest` (skips on SQLite, runs in CI).

## 31. Regression requirements
33. Suites `tests/Feature/RmeManualPricing/*` (Invoice, Correction, Governance, BranchBoundary; token
    `RmeManualPricing`) are declared in
    `config/ci_runner.php` `critical_gate_mandatory_suites`. Superseded tests in
    `RmeTariffAuthority*` / `RmeInvoiceCorrectionTariffAuthorityTest` were REVISED in place with a
    `REVISED by` note — never deleted.

## 32–33. Production deployment & rollback
34. No migration, no seeder, no permission change. Deploy with `scripts/deploy-vps-runner.sh` executed
    INSIDE the VPS. Production verification is read-only; never create a fake invoice, payment or
    correction. Rollback = code rollback to the previous GO; no data change to undo (no row was written
    by the release itself).

## 34. GO acceptance
35. Full tag `revision-rme-manual-pricing-authority-1-go` only when: revised D21 recorded, mandatory tariff
    dependency removed and verified, money validation intact, correction compatibility proven, Rp0 safety
    intact, D1/D7/D10 intact, flag OFF, security review PASS, regression PASS, rules synced, required CI
    PASS, merge verified, VPS deploy `exit=0` + `DEPLOY OK`, production verification PASS. A skipped Full
    Suite is reported as SKIPPED, never PASS.
